Below is a summary of what’s happening and two small fixes that together restore your drill-down overlays when you deep-link into a subprocess with the multi-diagram plugin:

1) Problem #1 – new BPMNPlane nodes created for each collapsed subprocess do **not** get the “_plane” suffix on their `id`.  
   DrilldownOverlayBehavior uses  
     canvas.findRoot( getPlaneIdFromShape(el) )  
   where getPlaneIdFromShape(el) = `el.id + '_plane'`.  
   Because your SubprocessCompatibility.createDiagram never assigned that `id`, `findRoot` returns `undefined` → overlays are never shown.

2) Problem #2 – DrilldownOverlayBehavior only adds its overlays on `import.done`.  Deep linking into a subprocess happens **after** initial import, so you also have to re-add (and re-show) all overlays whenever the root changes (i.e. on deep-link / setRoot).

Below are two small *SEARCH/REPLACE* patches.  The first one adds the proper `id` on each created plane, the second one hooks the `root.set` event to re-add/re-update overlays after deep-linking.

